Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Test Description,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Impacted Registers,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
1,GPIO,Register Write Read Verification,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test verifies the reset default values and write-read functionality of 23 GPIO per-pin registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_30) and additional group registers. The test first reads each register after reset and compares the value (masked with 0xFFFFFFFE to exclude bit 0) against the expected default value. Then it performs write-read verification using six distinct data patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), applying write masks before writing and read masks after reading. The expected read-back value accounts for read-only and write-only field behavior using the register field masks. Certain registers are skipped based on skip arrays, particularly VRRW-type registers. The test passes only if all default value checks and all write-read checks succeed with zero failures.",NA,Polling,0x0,0x58,"The soft reset check function is disabled via preprocessor conditional compilation and is not executed. VRRW-type group registers at offsets 0x80 and beyond are skipped during write-read testing via the skip array. The data_in bit (bit 0) is masked out during default value comparison because its value depends on the external pin state. The test requires the GPIO block to be out of reset (hreset_n deasserted) before execution. Register field types RO and WO are accounted for via read and write masks respectively. The test covers 49 register entries including group registers defined in the GPIO header files.","1. Initialize the GPIO IP and ensure the hardware reset signal is deasserted.
2. Read each of the 23 per-pin GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_30) and additional group registers after reset.
3. Mask out the data_in bit (bit 0) from the read value and compare against the expected default reset value for each register.
4. Skip registers flagged in the reset-skip array (VRRW-type group registers).
5. Verify that all readable registers return their expected default values; log any mismatches.
6. Write the first test pattern (0xFFFFFFFF) to all writable registers, applying the appropriate write mask for each register.
7. Read back each written register, apply the read mask, and compute the expected value accounting for read-only bits retaining default values and write-only bits not being readable.
8. Compare the read-back value against the computed expected value; log any mismatches.
9. Repeat steps 6-8 for the remaining five test patterns: 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, and 0xFFFF0000.
10. Skip registers flagged in the write-read skip array during all write-read iterations.
11. Verify that the total default-value failure count and write-read failure count are both zero.
12. Report PASS if all checks succeed with zero failures; report FAIL otherwise.","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10; gp0_gpio_11; gp0_gpio_12; gp0_gpio_13; gp0_gpio_14; gp0_gpio_15; gp0_gpio_16; gp0_gpio_17; gp0_gpio_18; gp0_gpio_19; gp0_gpio_20; gp0_gpio_21; gp0_gpio_22; gp0_gpio_23; gp0_gpio_24; gp0_gpio_25; gp0_gpio_26; gp0_gpio_27; gp0_gpio_28; gp0_gpio_29; gp0_gpio_30","PASS: All GPIO per-pin registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_30) and group registers return their expected default reset values after masking out the data_in bit (bit 0). All six write-read patterns produce the expected read-back values when accounting for read-only bits retaining defaults and write-only bits not being readable. Both the default-value failure count and the write-read failure count must be zero. FAIL: Any register returns an unexpected default value, or any write-read pattern produces a mismatched read-back value, resulting in a non-zero failure count.",Not,"This testcase validates GPIO register reset defaults and write-read integrity across 49 register entries (23 per-pin registers MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 through MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_30 plus additional group registers defined via gpio_def.h and gpio_offset.h headers). The test_case() function calls chk_rst_val() followed by chk_rd_wr(). chk_rst_val() iterates over addr_array[CNT] (CNT=49), skips entries where skip_rst_array[i]==1 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, reads each register via read_reg(addr), masks with 0xfffffffe to exclude data_in bit 0, and compares against default_value_array[i]. Any mismatch increments def_fail_cnt. chk_rd_wr() iterates over 6 write patterns in chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}. For each pattern, it writes (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) to each register (skipping entries where skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000), then reads back (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]) and computes expected value as ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])) where wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff). Any mismatch increments wr_fail_cnt. Final verdict: finish(0) if def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0, else finish(1). soft_reset_chk() exists but is disabled via #ifdef 0 block and uses SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS (0x00000000) and SOFT_RST_REG_DATA (0x00000000). Each gp0_gpio_X register has fields: data_in (bit 0, RO, reset 0), intr_raw_sts (bit 1, RO, reset 0), intr_clr (bit 16, WO, reset 0), pedge_intr_en (bit 17, RW, reset 0), nedge_intr_en (bit 18, RW, reset 0), level_sel (bit 19, RW, reset 0), io_ctrl (bit 20, RW2, reset 1), dout (bit 21, RW2, reset 0).","1. Entry: test_case() is called.
2. chk_rst_val() is invoked to check reset default values.
3. Loop i=0 to CNT-1 (CNT=49) over addr_array[i].
4. If skip_rst_array[i]==1, skip this register (continue).
5. If read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip this register as not readable (continue).
6. data_rd = read_reg(addr_array[i]).
7. data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe) masks out bit 0 (data_in, RO, pin-dependent).
8. Compare data against default_value_array[i].
9. If match: PASS (logged under DEBUG_DISPLAY). If mismatch: def_fail_cnt++ and error printed.
10. After loop, DEBUG_DISPLAY prints end of default value check.
11. chk_rd_wr() is invoked for write-read verification.
12. chk_val[6] = {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}.
13. Outer loop j=0 to 5 over chk_val[j]. data_wr = chk_val[j].
14. Inner write loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr = addr_array[i].
15. If skip_array[i]==1, skip (continue).
16. If write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip as not writable (continue).
17. Else: write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])).
18. Inner read loop i=0 to CNT-1: addr = addr_array[i].
19. If skip_array[i]==1, skip (continue).
20. If write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip (continue).
21. If read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip as not readable (continue).
22. Else: data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]).
23. wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff) inverted write mask.
24. exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])).
25. Compare data_rd against exp_val.
26. If match: PASS. If mismatch: wr_fail_cnt++ and error printed.
27. After all 6 patterns complete, DEBUG_DISPLAY prints end of write-read check.
28. Final check: if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) then finish(1) [FAIL], else finish(0) [PASS].
29. soft_reset_chk() exists but is disabled via #ifdef 0.","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_28; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_29; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_30; SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS","PASS condition: def_fail_cnt == 0 AND wr_fail_cnt == 0, resulting in finish(0). Default value check PASS: (read_reg(addr) & 0xfffffffe) == default_value_array[i] for all non-skipped registers where read_mask_array[i] != 0x00000000 and skip_rst_array[i] != 1. Write-read check PASS: For each of 6 patterns chk_val[j] = {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}, after writing (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) to each register, the read-back value (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]) must equal ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])). FAIL condition: Any mismatch increments def_fail_cnt or wr_fail_cnt, and if either > 0, finish(1) is called.","#include <stdio.h>; #include <stdlib.h>; #include ""test_common.h""; #include ""test_define.c""; #include<gpio/gpio_def.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000; #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000; #define CNT 49","addr_array[49]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,...,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_30}; default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49]; skip_rst_array[49]; chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}"
2,GPIO,Level Select Interrupt Enable,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the GPIO level-sensitive interrupt functionality for all 32 GPIO pins (pins 8 through 39). It tests both active HIGH and active LOW level interrupt modes. For each GPIO pin, the test configures the pin in input mode with level interrupt enabled, enables the corresponding group interrupt, triggers the interrupt via an external SRAM write stimulus, and waits for the ISR to fire. In the ISR, the test verifies the per-pin interrupt raw status bit, the group interrupt status register, clears the interrupt, verifies the clear was successful, disables the group interrupt, confirms the group status is cleared, and clears the LSS sysreg interrupt status. The test passes only if all 64 interrupt cycles (32 active HIGH + 32 active LOW) complete without any errors.",NA,ISR,0x0,0x88,"The test requires GIC interrupt routing to be functional (IRQ 87 for GPIO0, IRQ 88 for GPIO1). The LSS sysreg interrupt enable must be configured before GPIO interrupts can propagate to the GIC. An external stimulus mechanism via SRAM write at address 0xA0243ffc is required to drive the GPIO pin levels. The test uses conditional compilation (#ifdef GPIO0/#ifdef GPIO1) to select the correct GPIO instance. The GPIO block must be out of reset (hreset_n deasserted) before execution. The test depends on the int_pend external variable being cleared by the ISR to exit the polling loop.","1. Enable the GIC interrupt line for the GPIO instance (IRQ 87 for GPIO0).
2. Enable the GPIO interrupt in the LSS sysreg interrupt enable register (intr_en1).
3. For each of the 32 GPIO pins (pins 8-39), configure the per-pin register in input mode with level interrupt enabled and level select set to active HIGH (bits 19 and 20 set).
4. Enable the corresponding bit in the group interrupt enable register (gp0_intr1_intr_en1).
5. Write the external stimulus value to the SRAM location to drive the GPIO pin HIGH.
6. Wait for the interrupt service routine to fire and clear the pending flag.
7. In the ISR, read the per-pin register and verify the interrupt raw status bit (bit 1) is set.
8. Read the group interrupt status register (gp0_intr1_intr_sts1) and verify the corresponding pin bit is set.
9. Clear the per-pin interrupt by writing to the interrupt clear bit (bit 16) of the per-pin register.
10. Read back the per-pin register and verify the interrupt was cleared successfully (expected value 0x100001).
11. Disable the group interrupt by writing 0x00000000 to the group interrupt enable register.
12. Read the group interrupt status register and verify it reads 0x0 (all cleared).
13. Clear the LSS sysreg raw status by writing the GPIO interrupt bit to the raw_stcr1 register.
14. Read back the LSS sysreg raw_stcr1 and verify the GPIO interrupt bit is cleared.
15. Clear the GIC interrupt line.
16. Repeat steps 3-15 for all 32 GPIO pins with active LOW level select (bit 19 cleared, bit 20 set), using inverted stimulus values.
17. Report PASS if test_err equals zero after all 64 iterations; report FAIL otherwise.","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_intr1_intr_en1; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1; raw_stcr1; intr_en1","PASS: All 64 interrupt test iterations (32 active HIGH + 32 active LOW) complete with test_err equal to zero. For each iteration: the per-pin interrupt raw status bit (bit 1) must be set when the interrupt fires, the group interrupt status bit for the corresponding pin must be set, the per-pin register must read 0x100001 after interrupt clear, the group interrupt status must read 0x0 after disabling the group interrupt enable, and the LSS sysreg raw status GPIO bit must be cleared after writing the clear value. FAIL: Any of the above checks fails, incrementing test_err to a non-zero value.",Not,"This testcase validates GPIO level-sensitive interrupt functionality across all 32 GPIO pins (8-39) for both active HIGH and active LOW level selection. test_case() enables GIC IRQ (87 for GPIO0 via GIC_EnableIRQ(87)), writes MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 with LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR to enable sysreg interrupt routing. Active HIGH loop (i=0 to 31): writes 0x00180000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) setting io_ctrl=1 (input mode), level_sel=1 (active HIGH), nedge_intr_en=1; writes (1<<i) to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 (offset 0x84) to enable group interrupt for pin i; writes 0xffffffff to 0xA0243ffc (SRAM stimulus); sets int_pend=1 and polls while(int_pend==1) with wait_on(10). Active LOW loop (i=0 to 31): writes 0x00100000 (io_ctrl=1, level_sel=0) to per-pin register; writes (1<<i) to group interrupt enable; writes ~(1<<i) to 0xA0243ffc; polls int_pend. Default_IRQHandler(): sets int_pend=0; writes 0xffffffff to 0xA0243ffc; reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4); checks (rdata & 0x2) != 0x0 for raw interrupt status; reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 (offset 0x88) and checks (rdata_grp & (1<<i)) != 0; writes 0x00110000 to per-pin register to clear interrupt (bit 16); reads back and checks rdata == 0x100001; writes 0x00000000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 to disable group interrupt; reads MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 and checks == 0x0; writes LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 and reads back to verify (rdata & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR) == 0; calls GIC_ClearIRQ(87). finish(test_err) at end.","1. test_case() entry. test_err = 0.
2. GIC_EnableIRQ(87) for GPIO0 instance.
3. write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR) to enable sysreg interrupt.
4. Active HIGH loop: for i=0 to 31:
5.   wr_val = 1<<i.
6.   write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), 0x00180000) - sets io_ctrl=1, level_sel=1, nedge_intr_en=1.
7.   wait_on(50).
8.   write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val) - enables group interrupt for pin i.
9.   wait_on(10).
10.  write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xffffffff) - SRAM stimulus to drive pin HIGH.
11.  int_pend = 1; while(int_pend == 1) { printf; wait_on(10); }.
12. wait_on(100).
13. Active LOW loop: for i=0 to 31:
14.  wr_val = 1<<i.
15.  write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), 0x00100000) - sets io_ctrl=1, level_sel=0.
16.  wait_on(50).
17.  write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val).
18.  wait_on(10).
19.  write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~(wr_val)) - inverted stimulus for active LOW.
20.  int_pend = 1; while(int_pend == 1) { printf; wait_on(10); }.
21. finish(test_err).
22. Default_IRQHandler():
23.  wr_val = 1<<i; int_pend = 0.
24.  write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xffffffff).
25.  rdata = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4)).
26.  if ((rdata & 0x2) != 0x0): raw interrupt status confirmed.
27.    rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1).
28.    if ((rdata_grp & (1<<i)) != 0): group interrupt confirmed. Else: test_err++.
29.    write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), 0x00110000) - clear interrupt bit 16.
30.    wait_on(20).
31.    rdata = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4)).
32.    if (rdata == 0x100001): interrupt cleared. Else: test_err++.
33.    write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0x00000000) - disable group interrupt.
34.    rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1).
35.    if (rdata_grp == 0x0): group cleared. Else: test_err++.
36.    write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR).
37.    rdata = read_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1).
38.    if ((rdata & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR) == 0): sysreg cleared. Else: test_err++.
39.  else: Interrupt not occurred. test_err++.
40.  GIC_ClearIRQ(87).","MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; 0xA0243ffc; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1","PASS condition: test_err == 0 at finish(test_err). Per-pin interrupt raw status check: (read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4)) & 0x2) != 0x0. Group interrupt status check: (read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) & (1<<i)) != 0. Interrupt clear check: read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4)) == 0x100001 after writing 0x00110000. Group interrupt disable check: read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) == 0x0 after writing 0x00000000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1. Sysreg clear check: (read_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1) & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR) == 0 after writing LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR. FAIL: Any check fails, test_err incremented, finish(test_err) called with non-zero value.","#include<lss_sysreg.h>; #include<stdio.h>; #include<test_define.c>; #include<test_common.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_def.h>; #include<gpio/gpio_offset.h>",#define CNT 49,"addr_array[49]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,...,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23}; default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49]"
